            "created_at": "2025-08-24T10:02:45.477799+00:00",
            "notes": "Long, long text here because there's no more notes for the rest of the rounds, since this build from now on depends on what you prefer, and on a per-game/enemy team comp basis.\n\n## POWERS\nPersonally, I prefer taking [Express Detonation](item_8da4cbad-78cb-4ebd-8bc4-8dc150afec95) this round, but I'll highlight reasons for taking the powers here, since they'll also be the same options for round 7:\n- [Express Detonation](item_8da4cbad-78cb-4ebd-8bc4-8dc150afec95): Quicker explosion times can really mess with players' muscle memory, and combined with [Dae-Hyun\u2019s Detonator](item_cf3e51e1-12c7-4d92-a68b-7742f98fe8fa) can make the ults tough to avoid - though more enclosed maps can make this less effective. \n- [Party Protector](item_1ef9061d-cfa4-4f4e-a262-ab1012438e69): This is a good ability if your main use for your bombs is a safe re-mech, as it'll give your baby D.Va a bunch of overhealth and thus ability to survive. Plus, it gives your teammates in LOS the same overhealth, which is never a bad thing. \n- [Ultrawide Matrix](item_403fe162-4a59-4a8e-8af9-5f83267228e8): Bigger DM and more DM for more effective use of [Facetanking](item_f8af63d1-1fd4-4758-86ce-96f1ef7ea1ea), and thus giving you more survivability. If you're willing to use an item slot for [Multi-Task Mod](item_40997c0f-a8e3-46ba-b312-34c0790d0e87), this can become even better. \n- [Stat Boost](item_d3ef725b-3183-417c-bc5a-76bfa21c6cc5): Similar idea to the last power, more DM uptime = more dmg DMed = more health regained. Keep in mind that with this power, your DM only recharges at all after about half a second after you've stopped using DM. This doesn't sound like a lot, but if you're trying to do quick [Tokki Slam](item_9e2b8c2e-ed2f-4ce9-8424-9c86664e3925)s, especially immediately after using DM, then this power might not be effective for you.\n\n## ITEMS\nThe four items in the base build you'll want to keep throughout, but the rest of your build depends on what you want, and what you think will be more effective in each game. Let me go over the items I'd recommend you pick between. (Most of these items have either some amount of armor or shields to further help your slam damage, and the ones that don't give you good enough pros I think they can be worth it):\n- [Crusader Hydraulics](item_b64cee07-ca32-405d-987e-868b415bbc09): Good as just additional dmg reduction, especially if the enemies are going super WP/AS based or you don't have enough for two purples, though [Ogundimu Reduction Field](item_b12daf48-069b-44c1-88fe-221cbcff664d) is pretty much a straight upgrade I'd recommend if you can afford the purple.\n- [Dae-Hyun\u2019s Detonator](item_cf3e51e1-12c7-4d92-a68b-7742f98fe8fa): Do not underestimate this item, especially with quicker bomb times via [Express Detonation](item_8da4cbad-78cb-4ebd-8bc4-8dc150afec95). I'd recommend taking it if you have that power.\n- [Ogundimu Reduction Field](item_b12daf48-069b-44c1-88fe-221cbcff664d): As a tank, especially a tank with a *lot* of health and who will be basically at melee range with the enemies as you slam into them, you're likely to stack instances of damage pretty quickly. This also stacks very fast against beams. \n- [Divine Intervention](item_b5148b7f-8529-4b1b-a90c-5d7cf13f8f0c): Against heroes who do big bursts of damage, like Rein or Cassidy, scaled with weapon power in stadium's late rounds this is good item that can add a lot to your survivability. (Do note, it's difficult to tell with the wording whether \"at once\" means from just one source of damage or in one instance of taking damage from multiple sources, but this item is good either way)\n- [Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f): One of the options more focused around upping your damage through something other than your [Tokki Slam](item_9e2b8c2e-ed2f-4ce9-8424-9c86664e3925). The slam scales quickly, but you're unlikely to one-shot a lot of heroes, especially if they take some survivability items, and with the way D.Va's guns work the addition AS of this item will be almost immediately applied as you shoot someone, so combined with the bit of extra armor it gives you it's a decent choice if you want more power in the ability to finish off targets with your gun. \n- [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f): This item is better if you went more the [Party Protector](item_1ef9061d-cfa4-4f4e-a262-ab1012438e69) route, as if I take [Express Detonation](item_8da4cbad-78cb-4ebd-8bc4-8dc150afec95) and [Dae-Hyun\u2019s Detonator](item_cf3e51e1-12c7-4d92-a68b-7742f98fe8fa) then I tend to sent those ults almost as soon as I get them, vs with party protector and saving them until your mech gets destroyed. This item combos well with the latter, as you charge your ult fast and keep a bunch of buffs. \n- [Multi-Task Mod](item_40997c0f-a8e3-46ba-b312-34c0790d0e87): The only purple item I'd highly recommend that doesn't give you any armor or shields, but the potential upsides are more than worth it. The other D.Va build I really like to run is based around this item and DM uptime, as there are a lot of characters in the game where if you walk at them while shooting and DMing they quite literally can't do anything to stop you. Fairness or lack of fun for the enemy aside, this can be *extremely* powerful, and frankly I would take this item over even [Eye of the Spider](item_bbaf01d7-340d-4199-b738-86a98d68fe9b), especially if you took one of the powers that gives you more DM, or even just facetanking. \n\nIf you wanted to purely focus on DPS from here, then take [Multi-Task Mod](item_40997c0f-a8e3-46ba-b312-34c0790d0e87) and [Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f) in your final two slots. [Eye of the Spider](item_bbaf01d7-340d-4199-b738-86a98d68fe9b) or even [El-sa'ka Supressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100) can be taken over [Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f) in some matches, but I'd usually lean towards WJ due to the extra armor and that AS feels really nice with D.Va.",
